<title>GERMANY: Dresdner says completes syndicate for Gazprom loan.</title>
<headline>Dresdner says completes syndicate for Gazprom loan.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Dresdner Bank said on Monday that a further 38 banks had joined an international consortium putting up a 2.5 billion dollar loan to Russia's ROA Gazprom.</p>
<p>The consortium, lead by Dresdner, is now made up of a total of 57 banks from 17 countries, completing the syndication of the loan, the German bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Gazprom will use the credit to finance the building of sections of the Jamal-Europa gas pipeline, Dresdner said.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
